M1'S MODELLED HISTORICAL COVERAGE, THE STORE EACH WEATHER BASIS WOULD NEED, AND CREDIBLE IMPROVEMENTS (weather_basis.py,
stream l3plane, MESHSAT-1357). PROTOTYPE DESIGN: nothing built, powered or measured. MODELED on a1elec's energy_two_pack.py
through energy_basis.py's set-up (pinned); every coverage figure is a MODELLED HISTORICAL COVERAGE, not a success
probability. The author's analysis, AI arithmetic; not a qualified review and not the independent check.

0. REPRODUCTION: this script's window runs reproduce energy_basis.out section 8's six counts, and its mean-day runs the six
   WE rows of section 5: yes

A. THE MODELLED HISTORICAL COVERAGE, EXACTLY
   dataset: PVGIS 5.2, the seriescalc API (https://re.jrc.ec.europa.eu/api/v5_2/seriescalc), radiation PVGIS-SARAH2, meteorology ERA5, horizon DEM-calculated; hourly averages,
     UTC, stamped at HH:11; the September rows filed as v2/vendor/solar/pvgis-series/pvgis-leiden-seriescalc-2005-2020-september-slope40-aspect0.json
   years: 2005 to 2020 (16 Septembers); the panel orientation: slope 40 degrees, azimuth 0 (south), latitude 52.160, longitude 4.497
   windows: 864 of 72 hours, one starting at 06:00 and one at 18:00 UTC on each of 1 to 27 September of each year, so they
     OVERLAP (starts 12 h apart); none crosses the month's end (the last window's last hour is 30 September 17:11 UTC);
     the series is used as PVGIS gives it, not scaled to the 2015 to 2020 monthly mean
   initial charge: both packs full (their aged usable energy) at each window's start; no carry-over between windows
   ageing: REQ-014's 80 percent of the cells' specification minimum (energy_inputs.yaml aged_80), the 3.00 V line with the
     5 percent reserve; pack temperatures: the base at +20 C, the lid at the window's own minimum air (T2m)
   load: PS-IDLE-SPEC 42.8 W at the pack terminals (POWER-THERMAL.md section 4), plus in every WE case the lid path's standby
     drain, 1.8 Wh over 72 h (reconcile_lid_panel.out NOTES), both split between the packs by capacity
   array: 400 Wp, four Renogy RNG-100DB-H in 2S2P, a 200 W stage window; each calendar day's own TYP or WAB ratio
   failure criteria, all three reported: STOP, the kit stops (both packs at their 3.00 V line: the model's M1 verdict);
     COMB, the two packs' combined lowest store at or under 4.2 Wh; EACH, either pack's own lowest store at or under 4.2 Wh
   the cases: WE, energy_basis.out 1c's restated WE (conditional on the stage 0.93, front end 0.93 and charge 0.95 declared);
     WE-LO, the same three at their brackets' lower ends (0.90, 0.90, 0.90); WE-MKR, the same three at the makers' readings
     (stage 0.965 and front end 0.978, curve_readings.out; charge 0.9924, the cell sheet's resistive bound, energy_basis.out 2):
     INFERRED readings of other circuits and an upper bound, not established; NOM, energy_basis.out 1c's nominal inputs

