B. THE STORE EACH WEATHER BASIS WOULD NEED (the owner's decision L3-OD6; ILLUSTRATIVE targets, not proposals)
   Method: for each window, the least lid pack (the base held at 4S6P) with which the window passes COMB at WE, by bisection
   on the lid's parallel count (a real number, so the store is continuous); the store it amounts to is the base's and the
   lid's usable energy at the window's own lid temperature (aged, to the 3.00 V line with the reserve, at the load's rate).
   A target of X % takes the X-th percentile of those stores over the 864 windows. The mean-day basis (SC-37) uses the same
   bisection on the reference day at 40/0, both starts.
   cells (MAKER, v2/vendor/battery/samsung-35e-orbtronic.pdf): 3.35 Ah minimum x 3.60 V nominal = 12.06 Wh a cell (3.1, 3.3); 50 g maximum (3.10); 65.25 mm high by
     18.55 mm across (3.11): 17.63 cm3 as a cylinder, 22.45 cm3 as its square footprint. Cells only: holders, protection
     boards, wiring and enclosures are not counted. Established places (a1mech README section 2's table; the base 4S6P,
     24 cells): lid A 39, B 56, C 61, so at most 60 (4S9P both kept), 80 (4S14P tablet out), 84 (4S15P QMX out) cells in 4S groups.
   the current stores at WE on the mean day (the model's usable at the reference lid temperature 13.23 C):
     4S9P both kept      60 cells, 723.6 Wh nominal, 502.6 Wh usable (0.695 of nominal: ageing 0.80, the 3.00 V line with the reserve,
                        rate and temperature, as the model computes them)
     4S14P tablet out    80 cells, 964.8 Wh nominal, 660.5 Wh usable (0.685 of nominal: ageing 0.80, the 3.00 V line with the reserve,
                        rate and temperature, as the model computes them)
     4S15P QMX out       84 cells, 1013.0 Wh nominal, 692.1 Wh usable (0.683 of nominal: ageing 0.80, the 3.00 V line with the reserve,
                        rate and temperature, as the model computes them)
   the allowances between nominal and usable, per pack of the 4S21P kit (energy_budget.py's Pack.usable_wh, its factors):
     base 4S6P at +20 C     0.141 A a cell: rate 1.000, temperature 1.000, mean voltage 3.624 V (1.007 of 3.60 V), to the 3.00 V line or the
                            5 % reserve 0.937, ageing 0.80: 0.755 of nominal, 218.4 Wh
     lid 4S15P at 13.23 C   0.141 A a cell: rate 1.000, temperature 0.867, mean voltage 3.624 V (1.007 of 3.60 V), to the 3.00 V line or the
                            5 % reserve 0.937, ageing 0.80: 0.655 of nominal, 473.7 Wh
   cell limits: charge at most 1.020 A a cell for cycle life (REQ-075; the sheet's 3.5), against U3's 3.968 A over 6 cells and
     U3B's 7.936 A over the lid's cells (0.529 A a cell at 4S15P, less for a larger lid); discharge far under the sheet's 8 A (3.8)

   Third issue (CHECK-2 minors 2 and 3): the cells are the percentile of each window's own cell count (the least 4S
   group that carries it), not the count of the window at the store's percentile; the multiples are given both in usable
   Wh (against the 4S21P kit at the reference lid temperature) and in cells (against its 84 cells, the physical quantity).
